  "liner": {
   "body_md": "## Setlist highlights\n\n- **Kings March**: earliest performance in the archive; rare: 5 archived performances [3]\n- **Sidekick**: earliest performance in the archive; rare: 3 archived performances [3]\n- **Millers Last Stand**: earliest performance in the archive; rare: 3 archived performances [3]\n- **Waves**: earliest performance in the archive; rare: 8 archived performances [3]\n- **Hottentrot**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [3]\n- **Nealization**: rare: 6 archived performances [3]\n- **Blues Jam**: back after 48 archived shows (1816 days); mythic rare: 2 archived performances [3]\n- **Boozer**: rare: 5 archived performances [3]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **Soulive2018-03-02.sbd.matrix.cafiero.flac16** (recommended): matrix (soundboard mixed with audience mics); 13 songs; 148 min [1]\n- **soulive2018-03-02**: source not stated; 12 songs; 149 min [2]. Said about its sound: A few tracks have digital noise caused by microphone stand bumps and grabs [2]\n\n## Around the show\n\n- John Scofield sat in as special guest from Hottentrot through the end of the set [1]\n- John Scofield played guitar as special guest on tracks 7 through 12 [2]\n- Lineup: Alan Evans on drums and vocals, Neil Evans on organ/keys and left-hand bass [2]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **Soulive2018-03-02.sbd.matrix.cafiero.flac16**: taped by Chris Cafiero; transferred by Rich Stoler; source: SBD/Audix M1255B's matrix > FOH Board > Tascam DR-100(16bit/44.1) [1]. Also: Soundboard/Audix M1255B matrix feeding from the front-of-house board, captured on a Tascam DR-100 at 16-bit/44.1; Recorded by Chris Cafiero, Little Feat archivist; transferred from SD card via Audacity and CD Wave to FLAC, uploaded by Rich Stoler [1]\n- **soulive2018-03-02**: taped by Chris Kantner; transferred by Chris Kantner; source: AKG CK63 hyper > JK Labs DVC > Tascam DR-70D (24bit/44.1Hz) - FOB, LOC, 7ft, ORTF [2]",
